===== 11. disk, and what the ClickHouse delayed-drop cost us
  /dev/sda1       339G  297G   42G  88% /
  CH store: 365M	/var/lib/clickhouse/store
  measured during the campaign: without DROP TABLE ... SYNC, three consecutive
  8 GB landings left 42 GB free -> 9.5 GB free, because ClickHouse keeps a
  dropped table's metadata (and its parts on disk) for
  database_atomic_delay_before_drop_table_sec = 480 s so UNDROP can find it.
  CH's own description of that setting says the delay is IGNORED for a SYNC
  drop; cmd_drop therefore drops SYNC, and the store went back to ~130 MB.
